  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Marichka has a sequence SSS containing brackets `(` and `)` and character `x`, such that the bracketed sequence is valid.\n\nA valid bracket sequence is a bracket sequence which can be transformed into a correct arithmetic expression by inserting characters `1` and `+` between the original characters of the sequence.\n\nFor example, the given sequence SSS could be equal to `(x)((x))x`, because `()(())` is valid. On the other hand, it cannot be equal to `)(x)` because `)()` is not valid.\n\nZenyk decided that in one step, he will:\n\n\nSelect any pair of adjacent elements of the sequence and swap them.\nHe wondered what is the **minimum** number of steps he needs to take, to get a valid bracket sequence with all `x` outside the brackets.\n\nYou can notice that in valid bracket sequence, each opening bracket will have corresponding closing one and vice versa.\n\nElement `x` is outside all brackets if there is no such pair of corresponding opening and closing brackets such that `x` lies inside it. For instance, in sequence `(()())x(())xx()` all `x` are outside, but in sequence `((x))x()`, the first `x` is inside and second `x` is outside.\n\nNote that the intermediate sequences do not have to be valid.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line contains the string SSS, a sequence of characters `(`, `)`, and `x`, such that the bracket sequence is valid.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint one integer — the minimum number of steps Zenyk needs to take, to get a valid bracket sequence with all `x` outside the brackets.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤1 \\le 1≤|S|≤104 \\le 10^4≤104",
      "The bracket sequence of string SSS is valid."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "x",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nx is already outside of brackets, as there are no brackets."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "(x)",
        "output": "1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nZenyk can swap the first two characters, getting string x(), where x is outside of brackets."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "(()x())",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nZenyk can swap the second and third characters, getting the string ()(x()), and then the third and fourth, getting the string ()x(()), where x is outside of brackets.\nIt can be shown that we cannot move x outside brackets in less than 222 operations."
      }
    ]
  },
